  "question": {
    "text": "Motion of a particle in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;plane is described by a set of following equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The path of the particle will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4zChm",
      "text": "circular",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "97aXv",
      "text": "helical",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "klO58",
      "text": "parabolic",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5WEDj",
      "text": "eliptical",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the path covered by particle is a circle.</p>",
